Let $\mathbf{n}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -6 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{n}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -12 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ be the normal vectors to the planes $3x - 6y + 2z + 5 = 0$ and $4x - 12y + 3z - 3 = 0,$ respectively.  Then the angle bisectors are parallel to the vectors
\[\mathbf{n}_1 + \mathbf{n}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -18 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}\]and
\[\mathbf{n}_1 - \mathbf{n}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 6 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.\][asy]
import three;

size(180);
currentprojection = perspective(6,3,2);

triple I = (1,0,0), J = (0,1,0), K = (0,0,1);
triple O = (0,-0.5,0), N1 = (3,-6,2), N2 = (4,-12,3), P = (-5,-1,-5), Q = P + 0.5*(N1 + N2), R = P + 0.5*(N1 - N2);

draw(surface((2*N1 + 2*N2)--(2*N1 - 2*N2)--(-2*N1 - 2*N2)--(-2*N1 + 2*N2)--cycle),paleyellow,nolight);
draw((2*N1 + 2*N2)--(2*N1 - 2*N2)--(-2*N1 - 2*N2)--(-2*N1 + 2*N2)--cycle);
draw((P + 0.8*(Q - P))--(P + 0.8*(Q - P) + 0.2*(P - Q) + 0.2*(R - Q))--(P + 0.8*(R - P) + 0.2*(P - R) + 0.2*(Q - R))--(P + 0.8*(R - P)));
draw((P + 0.2*(N1 + N2))--(P + 0.8*(N1 + N2)),green,Arrow3(6));
draw((P + 0.2*(N1 - N2))--(P + 0.8*(N1 - N2)),green,Arrow3(6));
draw((0,-1,0)--(7,-1,0),Arrow3(6));
draw((0,-1,0)--(0,2,0),Arrow3(6));
draw((0,-1,0)--(0,-1,5),Arrow3(6));
draw(O--N1,Arrow3(6));
draw(O--N2,Arrow3(6));

label("$\mathbf{n}_1$", N1, N);
label("$\mathbf{n}_2$", N2, E);
[/asy]

Thus, the equation of the plane is of the form
\[7x - 18y + 5z + D = 0\]or
\[-x + 6y - z + D = 0.\]If the plane passes through $(-5,-1,-5),$ then in the first case,
\[7(-5) - 18(-1) + 5(-5) + D = 0,\]so $D = 42.$  This leads to the equation $7x - 18y + 5z + 42 = 0.$

In the second case,
\[-(-5) + 6(-1) - (-5) + D = 0,\]so $D = -4.$  This leads to the equation $-x + 6y - z - 4 = 0.$

We check that the point $(-5,-1,-5)$ does not lie on the plane $3x - 6y + 2z + 5 = 0,$ so the equation of the desired plane is $\boxed{7x - 18y + 5z + 42 = 0}.$
TERMINATE

